# Trivy CVE allowlist.
#
# Entries here suppress findings until the listed date. After that, Trivy
# fails again until the line is removed or the date extended. Add a one-line
# justification above each entry. Re-check unfixed CVEs at most monthly.

# CVE-2026-31789: OpenSSL heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems via large
# X.509 certificates. Fix exists in libssl3 3.0.19-1~deb12u2 but the
# gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12 runtime image has not been rebuilt
# with the patched package yet. We run on amd64 (64-bit) only, so the
# 32-bit-only attack surface does not apply to our workload.
CVE-2026-31789 exp:2026-06-25

# CVE-2026-44431, CVE-2026-44432: urllib3 CRITICAL findings on Python 3.9.
# The fixes ship in urllib3 2.7.0, which requires Python 3.10+. The
# cloudnative-pg/postgresql:17 base image ships Python 3.9 and uses
# urllib3 only inside barman (the backup tool) for AWS / Azure / GCS
# blob storage clients. Our deployment does not configure barman against
# any external cloud storage so the urllib3 code paths are not reached.
# Revisit when cloudnative-pg moves to Python 3.10+ or backports the fix.
CVE-2026-44431 exp:2026-06-25
CVE-2026-44432 exp:2026-06-25
